^{″} & =-\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})+\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{1}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{1}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}y=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2}):$\n\n$$\n[-\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})+\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}{y}_{{p}_{1}}]+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}{y}_{{p}_{1}}=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})+\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\pi A=0 \\\\ \\pi B=6\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}A=0 \\\\ B=\\frac{6}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{1}}=\\frac{6x}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2}).\n$$" 13194139536061 true] [17592186381662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381663 13194139536061 true] [17592186381662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381664 13194139536061 true] [17592186381662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381665 13194139536061 true] [17592186381662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381666 13194139536061 true] [17592186381662 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139536061 true] [17592186381662 1041 "field-1" 13194139536061 true] [17592186381662 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381664 13194139536061 true] [17592186381662 1110 #uuid "abe806f4-60a3-5c2f-a80d-ba6977c66f38" 13194139536061 true] [17592186381663 1034 "n=4" 13194139536061 true] [17592186381663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536061 true] [17592186381663 1111 #uuid "e3b4b37f-3f6d-5374-a408-afc4606c7ab7" 13194139536061 true] [17592186381664 1034 "n=1" 13194139536061 true] [17592186381664 1103 #edb/ref